WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:03.073
Welcome! Can you introduce yourself?

2
00:00:04.165 --> 00:00:06.567
Hello! Thanks for having me today.

3
00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:10.131
My name is Sifeddine El Kadiri, final-year student

4
00:00:10.171 --> 00:00:13.074
majoring in finance and computer science.

5
00:00:13.114 --> 00:00:16.358
I’ve had many opportunities to pass interviews with schools abroad

6
00:00:16.398 --> 00:00:18.880
and with recruiting teams from different companies

7
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.583
when I was looking for a final-year internship.

8
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:24.135
And I’m here today to share my experience with you.

9
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:31.273
In our scene, Ayoub lists his strengths but gives a vague example.

10
00:00:31.313 --> 00:00:35.158
What do you think of his answer? And how would you improve it?

11
00:00:35.198 --> 00:00:40.503
So I think Ayoub lists good qualities,

12
00:00:40.543 --> 00:00:43.196
but he does not give the jury enough evidence.

13
00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.852
Saying “I’ve done a lot of projects”

14
00:00:48.892 --> 00:00:53.097
does not explain the challenge, his personal contribution or the results.

15
00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:57.081
From my interviews, I prepare examples from university projects.

16
00:00:57.121 --> 00:00:59.484
I organised each answer into four parts:

17
00:00:59.524 --> 00:01:03.668
situation, my responsibility, my actions and the results.

18
00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:06.851
For instance, instead of simply saying “I am a good team player”,

19
00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:10.295
you could say: “During group project, we were falling behind schedule.

20
00:01:10.335 --> 00:01:13.278
I was responsible for combining our work,

21
00:01:13.318 --> 00:01:18.244
so I organised a meeting to identify the problems and help resolve a technical issue.

22
00:01:18.284 --> 00:01:21.487
We submit our work and application on time.”

23
00:01:21.527 --> 00:01:25.411
In this example, the answer shows teamwork through specific actions.

24
00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.794
If you have an accurate number, include it.

25
00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.075
But don’t invent it.

26
00:01:29.115 --> 00:01:31.267
A clear outcome is useful too.

27
00:01:31.918 --> 00:01:36.043
So finally, my advice to you would be to prepare a few honest examples.

28
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.245
You don’t need years of experience.

29
00:01:38.285 --> 00:01:43.470
You just need a university project, a club activity or a volunteering experience

30
00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.403
can demonstrate your strengths.

31
00:01:48.055 --> 00:01:51.869
Perfect. Thank you for sharing your experience and advices.

32
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.815
You’re welcome. Thanks for having me today.
